dialogue tam
  node root tam "You're the one going on the Marrow. Everyone says so. Is it true?"
    > "How does everyone know?" -> know
    > "What do you do up here?" -> do
    > "Have you seen anything strange?" -> strange
    > "Maybe. Goodnight." -> bye
  node know tam "I sit on the wall and count the ships. That's my job. Everyone comes past the wall and everyone talks, and I'm small, so they forget I'm there."
    > "What do they say?" -> strange
    > "Good job." -> bye
  node do tam "I count the ships. Used to be nine or ten a week. Now it's three, and two of those are the same boat going back and forth because nobody else will."
    > "Which boat?" -> which
    > "That's a good tally." -> bye
  node which tam "The Marrow. Uncle Hobb's her bosun. He's got Dad on his arm, in ink."
    > "Where's your dad?" -> strange
    > "Goodnight, Tam." -> bye
  node strange tam "The Arcadia was the fastest thing that ever came round the headland. I timed her. Then she stopped coming round."
    > "She was my father's ship." -> captain
    > "I'm sorry." -> dad
    > "Lots of ships don't." -> dad
  node captain tam "You're the captain's? …Then you're not a stranger. You're on the tally."
    -> dad
  node dad tam "Dad went with her. Tam Hobb, able seaman. I'm Tam too; Mum says that way she only has to shout once."
    -> dad2
  node dad2 tam "Mum says I'm not to talk about it, so I tell strangers."
    > "I'll look for them. All of them." -> promise
    > "Goodnight, Tam." -> bye
  node promise tam "If you find Dad, tell him the tally's still running. Tell him I kept counting."
    > "I'll tell him." -> bye
  node bye tam "Goodnight. That's you counted."
  # Act IV: his father, home.
  node home tam "You found her! Dad came up the steps an hour ago. I counted him. Then I made him go down and come up again so I could count him twice."
    > "Did you tell him you kept counting?" if seen:tam.promise -> kept
    > "How many is that now?" -> many
    > "Goodnight, Tam." -> bye
  node kept tam "He's seen the tally. It's on the back of all Mum's recipes. She's very cross. She's also crying, so it's hard to tell which."
  node many tam "A hundred and thirty, and one ship. People are harder than ships. They won't stand still to be counted, and they keep hugging."
